    "evidence_text": "For the first 5 classifiers, we used their implementation from the SciKit Learn library in Python (scikit-learn.org).\n\nWe trained several multi-class multi-label classifiers on this dataset.\n\nPrecision, Recall and F-measure for this multi-label classification are computed using a strategy similar to the one described in  .\n\nWe hypothesize that a good summary of these multiple comments can be constructed by identifying a set of important text fragments or phrases.\n\nInitially, a set of candidate phrases is extracted from these comments and a subset of these candidate phrases is chosen as the final summary, using Integer Linear Programming (ILP).\n\nFor comparing performance of our ILP-based summarization algorithm, we explored a few summarization algorithms provided by the Sumy package.\n\nA common parameter which is required by all these algorithms is number of sentences keep in the final summary.\n\nAssuming a sentence is equivalent to roughly 3 phrases, for Sumy algorithms, we set number of sentences parameter to the ceiling of K/3.\n\nAlso, human evaluators preferred phrase-based summary generated by our approach to the other\n\nsentence-based summaries.\n\nFinally, we proposed an ILP-based summarization technique to produce a summary of peer feedback comments for a given employee and compared it with manual summaries.",
